1
00:00:07,225 --> 00:00:09,155
Last time, we left you a dare.

2
00:00:09,405 --> 00:00:11,285
Millions of kinds of living things.

3
00:00:11,495 --> 00:00:14,245
But scientists sort them into only four groups.

4
00:00:14,302 --> 00:00:15,022
Easy!

5
00:00:15,072 --> 00:00:17,832
Big ones, small ones, green ones, and scary ones!

6
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:18,885
Hmm.

7
00:00:19,115 --> 00:00:20,365
Is Basil right?

8
00:00:20,575 --> 00:00:22,015
Did you lock in your four?

9
00:00:22,245 --> 00:00:24,245
Let's open the crates and find out.

10
00:00:24,759 --> 00:00:26,319
It's You against the Buddies.

11
00:00:26,539 --> 00:00:27,819
You lock in first.

12
00:00:28,039 --> 00:00:29,769
One finger for every point.

13
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:31,519
And a lizard is hiding.

14
00:00:31,749 --> 00:00:32,579
Find it!

15
00:00:33,019 --> 00:00:34,309
Look around this farm.

16
00:00:34,639 --> 00:00:35,369
A hen.

17
00:00:35,669 --> 00:00:36,479
A cat.

18
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:38,019
A tomato plant.

19
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:39,129
A fern.

20
00:00:39,419 --> 00:00:40,329
A mushroom.

21
00:00:40,629 --> 00:00:42,039
So many living things!

22
00:00:42,319 --> 00:00:44,219
How can scientists study them all?

23
00:00:44,281 --> 00:00:46,431
Put the ones that are alike together!

24
00:00:46,478 --> 00:00:47,398
Yes, Pip!

25
00:00:47,628 --> 00:00:50,908
Scientists look for what is the same, and what is different.

26
00:00:51,645 --> 00:00:52,855
Say it with me!

27
00:00:53,570 --> 00:00:57,940
The grouping of living things based on their similarities and differences is

28
00:00:57,690 --> 00:00:59,230
called classification.

29
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:08,340
Are you ready?

30
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:09,520
Three!

31
00:01:09,910 --> 00:01:10,550
Two!

32
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,550
One!

33
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:12,620
Go!

34
00:01:14,003 --> 00:01:14,873
Round one.

35
00:01:15,123 --> 00:01:18,703
Scientists classify living things into four main groups.

36
00:01:18,903 --> 00:01:20,293
Crate one: plants.

37
00:01:20,503 --> 00:01:22,163
Crate two: animals.

38
00:01:22,383 --> 00:01:23,983
So where does a mushroom go?

39
00:01:24,213 --> 00:01:25,483
One, with the plants.

40
00:01:25,693 --> 00:01:27,163
Two, with the animals.

41
00:01:27,373 --> 00:01:29,163
Three, in a group of its own.

42
00:01:29,393 --> 00:01:30,813
Show me with your fingers.

43
00:01:36,282 --> 00:01:37,232
Locked in!

44
00:01:37,362 --> 00:01:37,912
One.

45
00:01:37,662 --> 00:01:40,322
It grows from the ground, like a plant.

46
00:01:40,372 --> 00:01:41,012
Two!

47
00:01:41,132 --> 00:01:42,332
It has no leaves.

48
00:01:42,372 --> 00:01:43,752
So it must be an animal!

49
00:01:43,855 --> 00:01:44,576
Three.

50
00:01:44,409 --> 00:01:46,091
It has no leaves.

51
00:01:45,934 --> 00:01:47,775
And it cannot walk.

52
00:01:48,398 --> 00:01:49,708
The answer is three.

53
00:01:49,938 --> 00:01:52,908
A mushroom is not a plant: it does not make its own

54
00:01:52,658 --> 00:01:53,338
food.

55
00:01:53,568 --> 00:01:55,098
And it is not an animal.

56
00:01:55,328 --> 00:01:57,718
Mushrooms belong to a group called fungi.

57
00:01:59,893 --> 00:02:00,953
Three fingers?

58
00:02:01,173 --> 00:02:02,333
One finger up!

59
00:02:02,909 --> 00:02:04,379
Three crates are open.

60
00:02:04,589 --> 00:02:05,369
Plants.

61
00:02:05,599 --> 00:02:06,429
Animals.

62
00:02:06,659 --> 00:02:07,439
Fungi.

63
00:02:07,699 --> 00:02:08,959
Now, crate four.

64
00:02:09,085 --> 00:02:10,055
It's empty!

65
00:02:10,105 --> 00:02:11,545
Just a scoop of soil.

66
00:02:11,669 --> 00:02:13,099
Look closer, Basil.

67
00:02:13,339 --> 00:02:14,439
Much closer.

68
00:02:14,669 --> 00:02:15,639
Shrink down.

69
00:02:15,869 --> 00:02:16,729
Quietly.

70
00:02:19,329 --> 00:02:20,619
You are getting smaller.

71
00:02:20,989 --> 00:02:22,339
As small as an ant.

72
00:02:23,224 --> 00:02:24,054
Smaller.

73
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:26,224
As small as a grain of sand.

74
00:02:27,116 --> 00:02:28,256
Smaller still.

75
00:02:29,779 --> 00:02:31,139
Now you can see them.

76
00:02:31,469 --> 00:02:33,739
Tiny living things, all around you.

77
00:02:34,664 --> 00:02:36,304
Some are shaped like rods.

78
00:02:36,884 --> 00:02:37,894
Some are round.

79
00:02:38,494 --> 00:02:39,714
Some are spirals.

80
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:43,410
They are too small to see with your eyes alone.

81
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,280
But they are living things.

82
00:02:47,804 --> 00:02:49,524
Crate four is not empty.

83
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,994
These tiny living things are bacteria.

84
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:56,010
Bacteria are tiny living things and they come in different shapes and

85
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:56,620
sizes.

86
00:02:59,185 --> 00:03:00,385
Say it with me!

87
00:03:01,097 --> 00:03:06,327
Living things can be classified into four main groups: plants, animals, fungi

88
00:03:06,077 --> 00:03:07,187
and bacteria.

89
00:03:09,308 --> 00:03:11,348
So not big, small, green and scary?

90
00:03:11,398 --> 00:03:12,448
No, Basil.

91
00:03:12,688 --> 00:03:15,228
Size and colour do not decide the group.

92
00:03:15,736 --> 00:03:19,626
Plants are living things that usually have leaves, stems and roots.

93
00:03:19,846 --> 00:03:22,816
They are able to make their own food when there is light.

94
00:03:23,324 --> 00:03:25,854
Animals are unable to make their own food.

95
00:03:26,064 --> 00:03:28,424
They depend on other living things for food.

96
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:31,100
My rule.

97
00:03:31,450 --> 00:03:33,400
If it is green, it is a plant.

98
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,510
A tomato plant: green.

99
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:36,950
A fern: green.

100
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:38,820
A grasshopper: green!

101
00:03:39,172 --> 00:03:40,642
Something is not right.

102
00:03:40,852 --> 00:03:42,952
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

103
00:03:43,172 --> 00:03:44,082
Hold on!

104
00:03:49,589 --> 00:03:50,699
Arms crossed?

105
00:03:50,919 --> 00:03:52,059
One finger up!

106
00:03:52,269 --> 00:03:53,779
A grasshopper is green.

107
00:03:53,989 --> 00:03:55,419
But it is an animal.

108
00:03:55,739 --> 00:03:57,819
It is unable to make its own food.

109
00:03:58,179 --> 00:03:59,259
It eats leaves.

110
00:03:59,697 --> 00:04:01,397
So colour is not the clue!

111
00:04:01,637 --> 00:04:03,967
I will ask: can it make its own food?

112
00:04:04,541 --> 00:04:05,921
Show me your score hand!

113
00:04:06,161 --> 00:04:07,141
More than one?

114
00:04:07,391 --> 00:04:08,651
You beat the Buddies.

115
00:04:08,871 --> 00:04:09,861
Two fingers?

116
00:04:10,091 --> 00:04:11,081
High five!

117
00:04:11,884 --> 00:04:13,244
Did you spot the lizard?

118
00:04:13,504 --> 00:04:14,874
It was on the water pipe.

119
00:04:15,124 --> 00:04:16,944
Which crate does a lizard go in?

120
00:04:17,144 --> 00:04:18,434
Tell someone at home.

121
00:04:19,234 --> 00:04:21,394
Let's read today's key words together!

122
00:04:21,634 --> 00:04:22,354
Ready?

123
00:04:22,694 --> 00:04:23,723
Classification.

124
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,410
Fungi.

125
00:04:27,706 --> 00:04:28,606
Bacteria.

126
00:04:30,043 --> 00:04:30,943
Well done!

127
00:04:31,991 --> 00:04:33,491
The plants crate is full.

128
00:04:33,701 --> 00:04:36,691
But scientists sort plants again, into two groups.

129
00:04:36,828 --> 00:04:37,418
Look!

130
00:04:37,618 --> 00:04:39,958
This chilli plant has no flowers today.

131
00:04:40,098 --> 00:04:41,088
Not one!

132
00:04:41,215 --> 00:04:42,575
No flowers today.

133
00:04:42,805 --> 00:04:44,495
So is it a flowering plant?

134
00:04:44,715 --> 00:04:46,205
Find out in Part Two!

135
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:48,727
Say it with us!

136
00:04:49,526 --> 00:04:50,236
Ready?

137
00:04:50,361 --> 00:04:50,981
One!

138
00:04:51,361 --> 00:04:52,041
two!

139
00:04:52,366 --> 00:04:53,541
Now you know!
